Found by the B036 lane, 2026-08-30. Split out of B036 because it is a
different SHAPE of fix.

## The gap
`RemovedApiUsage { member, hint }` (src/typecheck/checker.rs) flags API that
compiles clean today but is a deprecated no-op at runtime. B036 added a
structured `replacement: Option<String>` to that variant so a fix can be
offered mechanically.

**The only `RemovedApiUsage` producer in the tree sets it to `None`**, on
purpose. Both hardcoded sites (checker.rs ~:230 and ~:2097) report
`awaitable.WithRunContext` with the hint "Use Meta::StartWithRunContext
instead" — and that migration is NOT a span swap:

    startnew(Worker).WithRunContext(ctx)     // before
    Meta::StartWithRunContext(ctx, Worker)   // after

`Meta::StartWithRunContext` is a FREE FUNCTION, and the receiver has to move
into the argument list. Replacing the member span would emit
`Meta::StartWithRunContext(ctx)` and **silently drop the coroutine** — a fix
that quietly deletes the user's work, which is far worse than offering none.
So B036 correctly ships the mechanism, the guard, and the
never-offer-what-you-cannot-make behaviour, with no live fix.

## Work
Offer a real quick fix for this migration, as a call restructure:
- Match the diagnosed `WithRunContext` member call.
- Locate the receiver expression and the argument list.
- Rewrite to `Meta::StartWithRunContext(<args>, <receiver-inner>)`, where
  `<receiver-inner>` is the coroutine passed to `startnew(...)` when the
  receiver has that shape.
- **Withhold the fix whenever the receiver is not recognisably a
  `startnew(...)` call**, rather than guessing. The whole reason this is a
  separate ticket is that a wrong rewrite here is silent data loss.

Determine the exact target signature from the Openplanet docs before
implementing — argument ORDER matters and must not be inferred from the
example above. Cite the source in a comment.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Red: `startnew(Worker).WithRunContext(ctx)` -> a quickfix is offered whose
applied edit is `Meta::StartWithRunContext(ctx, Worker)` and which re-parses
clean.

Variants (per CLAUDE.md, generalize):
- receiver `startnew(Worker)` with a coroutine IDENTIFIER, with a method
  reference `this.M`, and with a funcdef-typed expression
- `startnew` with extra arguments -> all carried through in the right order
- receiver NOT a `startnew(...)` call (a stored handle, a function result) ->
  **NO action offered** (the load-bearing negative case)
- the call chained further (`startnew(W).WithRunContext(c).Something()`) ->
  no action, or a correct rewrite; decide and document, do not guess
- multi-line call spanning several lines -> edit preserves surrounding layout
- two such calls on one line -> only the diagnosed one is edited
- the diagnostic still fires when no fix is offered (never suppress the
  warning just because the fix is unavailable)
- assert the result RE-PARSES, not merely that the text matches

## Gate
FP fixtures byte-identical — this adds an action, not a diagnostic. Compare
two binaries on the same machine at the same time.

## Related
B036 (added `replacement`, set `None` here), B035 (the fix seam), B047 (the
two producer paths).